# RidgeRunner solver output after the SP07 move. The old rules were anchored to
# KnotPlot/, so relocating ridgerunner silently un-ignored ~4 GB including nine files
# over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit. Note *.A.dat does NOT match a file literally named
# A.dat, so the directory rules are what actually protect this.
**/ridgerunner/out/
03_data/D_generated/knotplot_campaign_outputs/
A.dat
A.mat

# KnotPlot campaign solver output after the SP07 move. The old rule was anchored to
# KnotPlot/**/out/, so relocating the campaigns into 01_research silently un-ignored
# their out/ trees (~70 MB across 18 directories).
01_research/E_pipelines/E002_knotplot_multidynamics_relaxation_matrix/**/out/
01_research/E_pipelines/E003_knotplot_trefoil_seed_campaign/**/out/
01_research/E_pipelines/E004_trefoil_balance_point_campaign/**/out/
01_research/E_pipelines/E006_knotplot_multitopology_qhp_sweep/**/out/
01_research/D_benchmarks/D008_knotplot_missingparameter_certification/**/out/
01_research/D_benchmarks/D009_knotplot_parameter_atlas/**/out/

# RidgeRunner output is reachable through the KnotPlot/ridgerunner compat junction,
# which physically lands inside A002_ridgerunner. .git/info/exclude covers it once
# bootstrap_junctions has run, but that file is machine-local; a fresh clone needs the
# rule here too, before any junction exists.
04_tools/A_geometry/A002_ridgerunner/out/

# VortexLab spec-clock-proxy-decomposition campaign (2026-07-15..18, ~512 MB).
# Run output lives in the catalog where it belongs but stays out of git history, per
# the restructure invariant that outputs are runtime artifacts. Register a specific run
# explicitly if it becomes scientifically load-bearing.
03_data/D_generated/vortexlab_spec_clock_runs/
